A||N||6||DaRkLoRD||Calculating horsepower?||||5||
Z||000000||DaRkLoRD||07-03-2000||09:45 PM||||I've been wondering.. how is horsepower calculated? I know it can be measured with a dyno, but I was wondering if there's a way to figure it out based on RPM, acceleration etc? preferably in realtime, instead of plugging numbers into a computer program..<P>anyone got a formula/equation for this?<P>thanks!<P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||batboy||07-03-2000||10:35 PM||||If you know vehicle weight, 1/4 mile time and speed, you can calculate horsepower.||||reg||1
Z||000002||batboy||07-03-2000||10:38 PM|||| <A HREF="http://members.aol.com/topfiero/math.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://members.aol.com/topfiero/math.htm</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||olympic||07-03-2000||11:29 PM||||  Horsepower is a function of torque(lbs-ft) and rpm.  <P>HP=torque * rpm/5252<P>If you look at any HP and Torque vs RPM graph you will notice that the two lines always intersect at 5252 rpm.<P>Those calculators batboy posted are real handy.  Im not positive but I think any HP numbers used in those calculators are rear- wheel horse power.  They also assume optimal traction and gear ratios.<P>------------------<BR>"Born free....taxed to death."||||reg||1
Z||000004||FieroGTGirl||07-03-2000||11:33 PM||||<B>WHAT?</B><P>And I really believed you guys about all those stickers on the car...I thought you guys found a "cheap" way to get more horse power out of a car.<P>There goes all my ideas out the window...<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Kristina_1.JPG"> ||||reg||12
Z||000005||DaRkLoRD||07-03-2000||11:47 PM||||Hmm.. and how would extra weight in the car (full fuel tank.. a passenger.. luggage) affect this?<P>I'm basically thinking of a realtime display of the car's HP.. just cause I think it'd be a cool gadget.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A> ||||reg||1
